x86_64-linux  cxx1 writes the C1 forms of H's implicit constructor and destructor where clang emits only the C2 ones. Every special member this case writes by hand is defined out of line for exactly this reason, and `struct H { M m; };` is the one shape that cannot be: its constructor and destructor are the ones the *compiler* writes, which are inline by nature and have no out-of-line form to switch to - and running them is the whole point of that shape, since a member reached through an implicit destructor is the path that works where a written destructor's does not. The same difference implicit-move.nonames records, and docs/CONFORMANCE.md under "An inline member function is a strong symbol". x86_64-windows agrees on all 29 names and arm64-darwin on all 30.
